(Bug #102: `Create a list called NAME.` - a no-initializer declaration -
 gives NAME the type's default value []. The codegen default path
 synthesizes an empty list literal, which emits HEAP_ALLOC; previously no
 dependency was recorded, so heap.asm was never included and NASM failed
 on the bare macro. This program's only heap use is those bare
 declarations, so it reproduces the failure. The map default (allocated by
 _map_new, not HEAP_ALLOC) and a list declared inside a branch body
 (bug #25) must keep working.)

Create a list called items.
Create a map called lookup.
Print items.
Print lookup.

a number called n is 0.
While n is greater than 5,
    a list called in_branch.
Print in_branch.

a list called bare.
append 1 to bare.
Print bare.
Print bare's length.
